  "faq": "Frequently asked questions",
  "faqSubtitle": "Encryption, unlock, sync, backups, and more",
  "faqEncryptionQ": "Is my data encrypted?",
  "faqEncryptionA": "Yes. OpenKey encrypts your vault end-to-end on this device. Your master password and vault key never leave the device in plaintext.",
  "faqForgotPasswordQ": "What if I forget my master password?",
  "faqForgotPasswordA": "There is no recovery without your master password. Because encryption is zero-knowledge, OpenKey cannot reset it. Keep a secure backup of your password.",
  "faqOfflineQ": "Does OpenKey work offline?",
  "faqOfflineA": "Yes. Your vault is stored locally and unlocks without a network connection. An optional server is only needed for sync and sharing.",
  "faqAutoLockQ": "How does auto-lock work?",
  "faqAutoLockA": "When you leave the app without closing it, OpenKey counts how long you were away. After the time you choose in Settings, the vault locks and you’ll need your master password or biometrics to unlock again. Closing the app ends the session immediately.",
  "faqBiometricQ": "Is biometric unlock safe?",
  "faqBiometricA": "Yes. Biometrics unlock a key stored in the device secure hardware. Your master password is never replaced — you can still unlock with it anytime.",
  "faqSyncQ": "What is self-hosted sync?",
  "faqSyncA": "You can run your own OpenKey server. Devices send encrypted vault data so they stay in sync remotely. The server stores ciphertext only and never sees plaintext secrets. Your master password stays on each device.",
  "faqBackupQ": "How does Backup & Restore work?",
  "faqBackupA": "In Settings → Backup & Restore you can save a full vault copy to this device. OpenKey packs the database, app settings, and attachments into a compressed file, then encrypts it with your vault key (.okbak). Nobody can read the file without your master password. Restore decrypts that file and replaces the local vault with the backup — so keep the password and the .okbak file somewhere safe.",
